Date: Tue, 30 Sep 2025 13:45:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 767/913] dts: stm32: set ck_ker_lvdsphy to 13.5Mhz on stm32mp2
 boards

Ck_ker_lvdsphy clock is very sensitive to noise, which creates "PLL lock"
issue when the boards are heavily loaded (mouse, hard drive, etc.).
To remove this problem, the best way is to reduce this frequency.
13.5 MHz is a nice frequency for programming the pixel clock rate
without calculation errors.

